; quill run loads each raven package installed beside quill, so its output
; depends on the install tree: a package missing from it is skipped, and one
; built in another profile, such as a sanitizer's, may not load. The tests
; depend on the workspace's whole install tree, which builds every package in
; the current profile. A dependency on each preloaded package would name
; packages that a build of quill alone (dune build -p quill) does not define,
; and dune refuses it there. The tree also holds quill's stub libraries, which
; the bytecode executable loads at startup.

(cram
 (package quill)
 (deps
  (alias_rec %{workspace_root}/install)))

; preload.t puts packages first on OCAMLPATH, whose separator and paths
; differ on Windows.

(cram
 (applies_to preload)
 (enabled_if
  (<> %{os_type} Win32)))
